Now AgendaOperacional in agenda-operacional.component.ts. Changes:
- imports: add EstadoListaComponent, orientacaoVazia, classificarLista, parametrosFiltrosUrl, selecaoValida, FiltroAtivo. Also Router/ActivatedRoute for URL persistence.
- Add URL sync for `data` and `profissionalFiltro`.
- Add distinct states + actions:
  - empty state: use component with orientacaoVazia('recepcao-sem-atendimentos'); actions "Agendar atendimento" (scroll to create section) and "Alterar período" (focus data input).
  - loading state: component.
- Add chips for active filters + clear.

Current decorator imports: `[CommonModule, FormsModule, RouterLink, UiIconComponent]`. Add EstadoListaComponent.

Current section:
```
      <section class="surface-panel section-card">
        <div class="section-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Atendimentos</p><h2>Dia selecionado</h2></div>
          <app-icon name="calendar" /></div>
        <p class="muted-copy">Confirme atendimentos e acompanhe a agenda desta filial no dia escolhido.</p>
        <div class="form-grid">
          <label>Data <input type="date" [(ngModel)]="data" (change)="carregar()"></label>
          <label>Profissional
            <select [(ngModel)]="profissionalFiltro" (change)="carregar()">
              <option [ngValue]="null">Todos</option>
              @for (p of profissionais(); track p.id) { <option [ngValue]="p.id">{{ p.nome }}</option> }
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>
        @if (carregando()) { <p role="status">Carregando agenda…</p> }
        @else if (!itens().length) { <p class="muted-copy">Sem atendimentos nesta data.</p> }
        <div class="user-list">
          @for (item of itens(); track item.id) { ... }
        </div>
      </section>
```

New:
```
      <section id="atendimentos" class="surface-panel section-card">
        ...
        <div class="form-grid">
          <label>Data <input #filtroData type="date" [ngModel]="data" (ngModelChange)="aplicarData($event)"></label>
          <label>Profissional
            <select [ngModel]="profissionalFiltro" (ngModelChange)="aplicarProfissional($event)">
              <option [ngValue]="null">Todos</option>
              @for (p of profissionais(); track p.id) { <option [ngValue]="p.id">{{ p.nome }}</option> }
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>
        @if (chipsFiltros().length) {
          <div class="filtros-resumo">
            <span class="eyebrow">Filtros ativos</span>
            @for (chip of chipsFiltros(); track chip.chave) { <span class="filtro-chip">{{ chip.rotulo }}: {{ chip.valor }}</span> }
            <button class="button ghost small" type="button" (click)="limparFiltros()">Limpar filtros</button>
          </div>
        }
        @if (estadoAgenda() === 'carregando') {
          <app-estado-lista [estado]="'carregando'" [titulo]="'Carregando agenda…'" />
        } @else if (estadoAgenda() === 'erro') {
          <app-estado-lista [estado]="'erro'" [titulo]="'Não foi possível carregar a agenda'"
            [descricao]="erro()" [icone]="'calendar'">
            <button class="button primary" type="button" (click)="carregar()">Tentar novamente</button>
          </app-estado-lista>
        } @else if (estadoAgenda() !== 'conteudo') {
          <app-estado-lista [estado]="estadoAgenda()" [titulo]="vazio().titulo"
            [descricao]="vazio().descricao" [icone]="'calendar'">
            <button class="button primary" type="button" (click)="agendarAtendimento()">Agendar atendimento</button>
            <button class="button ghost" type="button" (click)="focarPeriodo()">Alterar período</button>
          </app-estado-lista>
        }
        <div class="user-list"> ... </div>
      </section>
```

Wait: if estado is erro, then `erro()` is displayed in the component AND the top `@if (erro()) { <p class="notice error"...> }`. Duplicate. Since AgendaOperacional uses `erro()` for many things (creation errors, loading), showing it in the component for the agenda load specifically. But the top notice always shows erro. Let me keep the top notice and NOT show erro in the component; instead the component erro branch would duplicate. Hmm.

Option: remove the top `@if (erro())` and rely on component? But erro is used for creation section too. Better: add a dedicated `erroAgenda` signal for the list load, keep `erro()` for mutations. That's cleaner.

Let me add `readonly erroAgenda = signal('')`. In `carregar()`: on error set erroAgenda, on success clear. Then `estadoAgenda()` uses erroAgenda. And stop setting `erro` in carregar (use erroAgenda). Top notice keeps for mutation errors.

Let me restructure carregar:
```
  carregar(): void {
    if (!this.unidadeId() || !this.data) { return; }
    this.carregando.set(true); this.erroAgenda.set('');
    this.api.filial(this.unidadeId(), this.data, this.data, this.profissionalFiltro ?? undefined).subscribe({
      next: lista => { this.itens.set(lista); this.carregando.set(false); },
      error: e => { this.erroAgenda.set(AuthService.mensagemErro(e)); this.carregando.set(false); }
    });
  }
```

estadoAgenda():
```
