  return classificarLista({ carregando: this.carregando(), erro: !!this.erroAgenda(),
    total: this.itens().length, filtrosAtivos: this.chipsFiltros().length });
}
```

chipsFiltros(): data always present (a filter), profissional optional. Hmm, "data" is a period selector, not exactly a filter. The SPEC says chips for "Filial: Centro", "Estado: Confirmado". For agenda, the professional filter is a filter; the date is the period. Showing "Data: 06/10/2026" as a chip and "Profissional: Ana" would be reasonable. But then filtrosAtivos >= 1 always, so empty always 'sem-resultado', never 'sem-dados'. The SPEC wants distinction: "sem dados" (nothing at all for the period) vs "sem resultado do filtro" (filter yielded nothing). For agenda, an empty day without professional filter is "sem dados"; with professional filter it's "sem-resultado". So exclude the date from "filtrosAtivos". Let me define chips for professional only (and maybe date). Actually the SPEC's agenda context says "Recepção sem atendimentos no período" → "Agendar atendimento" and "Alterar período". So the period is a navigation control. I'll treat `profissionalFiltro` as the filter for `filtrosAtivos`, and show a chip "Profissional: X" when set. And optionally a "Data: dd/mm" chip. To keep the sem-dados/sem-resultado distinction, `filtrosAtivos = profissionalFiltro ? 1 : 0`.

